1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,921
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:43,961
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,755
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS FILMED
IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:56,181
[exhales deeply]

7
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:00,227
[Changun] Joo.

8
00:01:01,228 --> 00:01:02,813
[in English] Would you like
something to drink?

9
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:05,941
[in Korean] You did a great job.

10
00:01:06,525 --> 00:01:08,193
You too, sir.

11
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:13,865
Working with you again
felt like old times.

12
00:01:13,949 --> 00:01:15,951
-[chuckles softly]
-I could really count on you.

13
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:17,119
Me too.

14
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,122
What did you think of Jin Isoo?

15
00:01:21,123 --> 00:01:22,249
[inhales deeply]

16
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:24,042
He can be a bit odd,

17
00:01:25,127 --> 00:01:26,712
and he's unpredictable,

18
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:29,590
but he's got good instincts.

19
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:31,383
And he's quite serious about the job.

20
00:01:31,967 --> 00:01:33,135
Right?

21
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:36,013
He's actually a decent detective.

22
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:39,725
Do you have someone lined up
to lead Team 1?

23
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:43,979
[inhales deeply]

24
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,147
No. [exhales]

25
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:47,024
No one.

26
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:52,863
So I was wondering...

27
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:56,199
Someone just like you
would be perfect for the job.

28
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:58,577
Someone who's capable,

29
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,580
can manage Detective Jin,
and has real charisma.

30
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:05,667
Someone of that caliber

31
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,003
is really hard to come by.

32
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:11,131
[chuckles]

33
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:15,677
[Isoo] Hello!

34
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:17,137
[crowd cheering]

35
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:19,890
[cheers]

36
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,642
When did you have time to make these?

37
00:02:21,725 --> 00:02:23,727
Hi there! Want a photo?

38
00:02:24,728 --> 00:02:27,314
[Junyoung sighs]
He's going overboard again.

39
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:29,191
[Kyungjin] Come on, it's all good fun.

40
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:30,525
Okay, band.

41
00:02:30,609 --> 00:02:31,693
Let's give it a try.

42
00:02:31,777 --> 00:02:33,445
Just like we practiced. Ready!

43
00:02:35,197 --> 00:02:36,281
[shouts command]

44
00:02:36,365 --> 00:02:38,158
[♪ triumphant brass fanfare playing]

45
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,626
-[in English] Stop!
-[Taegyun, in Korean] What in the world...

46
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,920
What is all this?

47
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:51,713
Sir!

48
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:54,841
Oh, for heaven's sake.

49
00:02:54,925 --> 00:02:57,219
-That good for nothing...
-Sir.

50
00:02:57,803 --> 00:03:00,097
Come on, clear all this out.
[exclaims scornfully]

51
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:02,641
-This was Jin Isoo's doing.
-Sir!

52
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:04,810
[Isoo] It's for my new boss.
You know the drill.

53
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:05,894
Let's do this.

54
00:03:08,772 --> 00:03:10,148
Somebody's working hard.

55
00:03:10,232 --> 00:03:12,734
Of course.
We're getting a new team leader.

56
00:03:12,818 --> 00:03:13,944
Of course.

57
00:03:15,362 --> 00:03:17,280
Oh. Incoming!

58
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:19,157
[♪ triumphant brass fanfare playing]

59
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:25,455
[engine shuts off]

60
00:03:26,498 --> 00:03:28,291
[music stops]

61
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:31,378
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

62
00:03:42,139 --> 00:03:43,181
Joo Hyera?

63
00:04:00,449 --> 00:04:02,409
I didn't expect such a grand welcome.

64
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:03,535
[chuckles softly]

65
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:07,038
Detective Jin has been busy
since this morning.

66
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:09,708
I guess you can be sweet.

67
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:13,628
This is the new team leader of Violent
Crime Investigation Team 1, Joo Hyera.

68
00:04:15,005 --> 00:04:16,548
She's got years on you boys.

69
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,218
She was on our Violent Crime Team
before moving to Counterterrorism.

70
00:04:20,302 --> 00:04:21,303
[chuckles softly]

71
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:24,514
Detective Jin, take good care
of your new boss.

72
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:27,392
Take good care of her.

73
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:33,732
Detective Jin Isoo,

74
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:37,194
Detective Park Junyoung,
Detective Choi Kyungjin.

75
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:38,653
Glad to join the team.

76
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:42,199
[muttering] This has to be a nightmare.

77
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,325
It's real.

78
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:45,410
Get used to it.

79
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:55,754
Looking forward to it, nutjob.

80
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:07,766
But why?

81
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:12,729
She has it good
in Counterterrorism, so why, huh?

82
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:13,939
That's true.

83
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:15,524
Why the sudden transfer?

84
00:05:15,607 --> 00:05:17,734
[sighs] I'm seriously doomed.

85
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:19,694
What are you talking about?

86
00:05:19,778 --> 00:05:21,947
She's a capable,
experienced veteran detective.

87
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:24,324
We don't get along.

88
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:25,951
She doesn't like me.

89
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:28,370
[♪ upbeat music playing]

90
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:29,913
Nutjob. Hey, nutjob.

91
00:05:31,665 --> 00:05:32,666
Hey, nutjob!

92
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:34,417
[tires screeching]

93
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:36,545
Hey, nutjob!

94
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:37,879
Hey, nutjob.

95
00:05:44,553 --> 00:05:45,637
[Junyoung] It's nothing new.

96
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,347
I didn't like you at first, either.

97
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,932
[chuckling]

98
00:05:50,809 --> 00:05:51,893
Sir!

99
00:05:51,977 --> 00:05:53,353
What?

100
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:54,729
So...

101
00:05:54,813 --> 00:05:56,857
About Detective Joo Hyera.

102
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,400
I heard she worked here before.

103
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:00,110
Yeah.

104
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:02,529
We worked together for about a year or so.

105
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:06,032
Then why did she come back here?

106
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:07,117
Beats me.

107
00:06:08,410 --> 00:06:09,411
Ah.

108
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,121
It must be to torment you.

109
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:13,707
[exclaims] Come on, be serious!

110
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:15,584
She's good at her job.

111
00:06:16,251 --> 00:06:18,044
She's pretty laid-back, so don't worry.

112
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:19,838
[♪ quirky music playing]

113
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:20,922
How old is she?

114
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:22,007
[inhales sharply]

115
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:23,967
Same age as you, I think.

116
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:25,468
-Same age as me?
-Yes.

117
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:31,683
By the way, don't ever make bets with her.

118
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:34,853
-Why not?
-She's kind of competitive...

119
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:37,188
No, she's insanely competitive.

120
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,065
She always has to win.

121
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:46,323
Hmm...

122
00:06:50,994 --> 00:06:52,454
[mouse clicks]

123
00:06:53,622 --> 00:06:55,832
-[game mine explodes]
-[sighs]

124
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,959
-[knock at door]
-Yes, come in.

125
00:07:00,295 --> 00:07:02,797
Oh, Detective Joo Hyera.
Come in and have a seat.

126
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,301
[Taegyun exhales]

127
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:10,013
I appreciate you
taking on this tough role.

128
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,264
[chuckles softly] Not at all.

129
00:07:11,348 --> 00:07:14,017
You also successfully closed
the bombing case.

130
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,435
We're lucky to have you.

131
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:17,312
You're too kind.

132
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:21,983
By the way,
I have one favor to ask of you.

133
00:07:22,651 --> 00:07:23,985
Of course. Please, go ahead.

134
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:26,237
It's about Jin Isoo.

135
00:07:27,364 --> 00:07:28,365
[sighs]

136
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:30,575
I can't sleep at night because of him.

137
00:07:30,659 --> 00:07:32,327
Strictly speaking,

138
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:36,539
those bombings wouldn't have happened
if it weren't for him.

139
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:40,877
What's a spoiled rich kid doing
running wild in the police force?

140
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:44,881
God knows what he did, but he won over
everyone in Violent Crime and Chief Park.

141
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:48,093
Discipline's gone to hell around here.

142
00:07:49,052 --> 00:07:51,805
Discipline's important in an organization.

143
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:54,182
Which is why

144
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:57,894
you should watch him,
and when he's about to cause trouble,

145
00:07:58,687 --> 00:08:01,106
report it to me.
I'll use it to kick him out.

146
00:08:02,524 --> 00:08:03,525
Yes, sir.

147
00:08:03,608 --> 00:08:05,985
Good. I'm counting on you.

148
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:08,488
I also have a favor to ask.

149
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,073
Yes, what is it?

150
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:11,741
Once Jin Isoo leaves,

151
00:08:11,825 --> 00:08:13,368
I'd like to pick his replacement.

152
00:08:14,119 --> 00:08:15,537
Sure, you do that.

153
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:16,621
Yes, sir.

154
00:08:33,847 --> 00:08:34,848
Detective Jin.

155
00:08:36,266 --> 00:08:37,267
Got something to say?

156
00:08:38,601 --> 00:08:39,686
[in English] Nope.

157
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,480
[in Korean] We can finish
the report tomorrow.

158
00:08:42,564 --> 00:08:43,565
Let's go out for drinks tonight.

159
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:44,649
Okay.

160
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:47,819
Then I know this celebrity chef...

161
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:49,988
Let's go somewhere local, in one hour.

162
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,489
Yes, ma'am.

163
00:08:56,286 --> 00:08:59,289
[muttering] She's the worst.
Seriously, the worst.

164
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,332
The absolute worst.

165
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:07,005
[♪ soft pop music playing in background]

166
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:11,843
Okay, let's make a toast.

167
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:17,724
[whispers] Bro.

168
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:23,354
-Here's to working together.
-Welcome to the team!

169
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:25,440
-Welcome.
-[Junyoung] Welcome.

170
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:30,737
[Hyera exhales]

171
00:09:34,032 --> 00:09:36,743
Chief Park?
He was my immediate supervisor.

172
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:38,703
Wow! What was he like?

173
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,747
[exhales] He was scary.

174
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:43,083
I learned a lot from him.

175
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:44,501
We heard so much about you.

176
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,503
-Like how you caught Kim Dusik.
-Kim Dusik?

177
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,421
[Junyoung] Yeah, a serial robber
and killer.

178
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:50,298
I heard you spent a week on stakeout.

179
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:52,133
[scoffs] People still talk about that?

180
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:53,426
Of course.

181
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:54,511
A whole week? Where?

182
00:09:55,637 --> 00:09:58,515
The convenience store
in front of his girlfriend's house.

183
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,682
I worked there.

184
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:02,185
I caught him
when he came to buy cigarettes at dawn.

185
00:10:02,268 --> 00:10:03,937
[exclaims]

186
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,021
But...

187
00:10:05,814 --> 00:10:08,399
[spluttering] ...why did you come back?

188
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:11,861
That's...

189
00:10:13,238 --> 00:10:14,489
No comment.

190
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:16,658
[muttering] "No comment," my foot.

191
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:18,326
[grunts]

192
00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:20,787
-Bro, where are you going?
-[Isoo] The restroom.

193
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:23,998
Then, tell us about the chief.

194
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:25,083
The chief?

195
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:27,085
What kind of stuff?

196
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:29,254
Something cool, or something dirty?

197
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:30,338
Something dirty.

198
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:32,006
[all chuckling]

199
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,175
It was summer, around five years ago.

200
00:10:34,259 --> 00:10:35,593
It was a scorching hot day.

201
00:10:35,677 --> 00:10:37,345
It turns out that bastard

202
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:39,556
was hiding in a pigsty.

203
00:10:40,223 --> 00:10:42,267
The chief just dove right in.

204
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,852
-[chuckles]
-[Junyoung] No way.

205
00:10:43,935 --> 00:10:45,186
The chief?

206
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:47,689
The stench was unbearable,
but we couldn't say a word.

207
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:50,859
His wife told him at the door
to strip down and throw it all away.

208
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:52,527
[all laughing]

209
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:56,030
I didn't expect that from him.

210
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:57,991
We didn't order these.

211
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:59,993
Ah. Over there.

212
00:11:02,871 --> 00:11:04,289
[♪ jaunty music playing]

213
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:05,790
[Kyungjin] No way!

214
00:11:05,874 --> 00:11:07,333
SCORE OVER 1,000
FOR 4 FREE BEERS

215
00:11:08,293 --> 00:11:10,003
Isoo scored over 1,000 points.

216
00:11:15,717 --> 00:11:18,678
[sighs] This isn't something
just anyone can do.

217
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,013
"Just anyone?"

218
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,974
You haven't seen the champion's photo yet?

219
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,058
Champion?

220
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:28,479
DART CHAMPION

221
00:11:29,272 --> 00:11:30,607
-Ooh.
-That's amazing.

222
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:32,984
[scoffs] Champion?

223
00:11:34,485 --> 00:11:36,738
I'm taking that champion's place today.

224
00:11:38,615 --> 00:11:39,699
-Ooh.
-Oh!

225
00:11:39,782 --> 00:11:41,743
-[Kyungjin] Great shot!
-[clapping]

226
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:42,827
Talk is cheap.

227
00:11:52,295 --> 00:11:54,047
[Kyungjin chuckles] So cool.

228
00:12:09,604 --> 00:12:10,813
[exhales]

229
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,783
Please could you stop them?

230
00:12:22,951 --> 00:12:23,952
We're sorry.

231
00:12:27,205 --> 00:12:28,748
[♪ quirky music playing]

232
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:30,375
You stepped on the line.

233
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:31,793
[Hyera] Okay, fine.

234
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,670
I thought he said they don't get along.

235
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:35,046
They get along really well.

236
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:37,340
-[grunts sharply]
-[exclaims in annoyance]

237
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:38,549
Oh!

238
00:12:38,633 --> 00:12:40,385
Detective Joo won.

239
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:42,720
No wonder she's the dart champion.
Now, let's go.

240
00:12:42,804 --> 00:12:44,097
-Come on.
-[Kyungjin] Great shot!

241
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:45,348
-Bro.
-Let's go.

242
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,975
[Isoo] I'm not going anywhere.

243
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:48,851
Oh!

244
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:50,645
The machine was so shocked, it broke.

245
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:51,729
[exclaims in dismay]

246
00:12:51,813 --> 00:12:54,190
Let's go. Come on.

247
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:56,734
Bro.

248
00:12:56,818 --> 00:12:58,152
Learn to accept defeat.

249
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,154
[Kyungjin] Come on.

250
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:05,076
Let's go.

251
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:12,250
[Isoo] Huh?

252
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:16,045
Ah, I'm a really great shot, too.

253
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:18,631
As great as me?

254
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:20,842
[scoffs]

255
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:22,677
[♪ dramatic music playing]

256
00:13:25,555 --> 00:13:26,639
[groans]

257
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:28,391
[sighs in exasperation]

258
00:13:42,572 --> 00:13:44,741
Learn to accept the results.

259
00:13:45,575 --> 00:13:46,659
That's a tiny kitten.

260
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:47,827
[laughs smugly]

261
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,792
[game announcer speaking in English]

262
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:58,254
-[game characters grunting]
-[frantic button-clicking]

263
00:14:01,049 --> 00:14:02,050
[exclaims]

264
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:08,222
[game announcer reads]

265
00:14:08,306 --> 00:14:09,766
[Junyoung and Kyungjin clapping]

266
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:16,731
[game characters grunting]

267
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:19,734
[frantic button-clicking]

268
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,950
-[game announcer reads]
-[exclaims]

269
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:34,290
[in Korean] Just one more round.

270
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:36,334
One round.

271
00:14:48,721 --> 00:14:50,723
[snoring]

272
00:14:50,807 --> 00:14:53,768
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

273
00:14:58,898 --> 00:14:59,899
Mmm.

274
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,027
[grunts groggily]

275
00:15:03,111 --> 00:15:04,112
[Junyoung] Morning.

276
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:06,656
Goodness, look at you.

277
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:07,782
[sighs heavily]

278
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:09,283
What time did you go home?

279
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,077
[sighs] Around 3:00 a.m.

280
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:14,163
Detective Joo must be really tired, too.

281
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:17,291
[groans]

282
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:19,001
[footsteps approaching]

283
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:20,670
[in English] Good morning.

284
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:22,338
[in Korean] Ma'am, are you all right?

285
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:23,673
[Hyera] Mmm? What do you mean?

286
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:25,842
Let's finish that report today.

287
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:27,260
-Yes, ma'am.
-Understood.

288
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,685
[sighs softly]

289
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:40,064
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

290
00:15:40,148 --> 00:15:41,607
[keyboard clacking]

291
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:46,988
AHIN

292
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:52,201
[mouse clicks]

293
00:15:53,452 --> 00:15:54,912
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

294
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:58,416
AHIN
THERE'S A GHOST IN THE ABANDONED HOUSE!

295
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:01,794
"Whatever it is, I'll take care of it."

296
00:16:01,878 --> 00:16:03,129
You startled me.

297
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:04,463
DETECTIVE JIN RESPONDING!

298
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:07,925
You think you're Batman?
Light a signal, why don't you?

299
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:11,971
[inhales]

300
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:15,349
Oh, I do give off that Batman vibe.

301
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,353
[scoffs] That's narcissism.
It's a disorder, you know.

302
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:23,357
[sighs] You probably don't know,
but I'm the cheat code for solving cases.

303
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:27,236
[sighs] You should really see me
out there in the field.

304
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,821
I believe I did.

305
00:16:28,905 --> 00:16:30,364
Frozen, after touching the bomb.

306
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:33,743
What's the report about?

307
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:37,622
[Ahin] There's a ghost
in the abandoned house.

308
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:41,918
My name is Park Ahin. I'm a middle school
student from Gangha 3-dong.

309
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:45,504
My dream is to become
a great police officer.

310
00:16:45,588 --> 00:16:49,050
That's why I have a habit of keeping
an eye out for anything suspicious.

311
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:51,928
But a few days ago,

312
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:56,933
I saw these eerie lights floating inside
the abandoned house across the street.

313
00:16:57,016 --> 00:17:00,937
There was a murder there,
so the house hasn't sold in years.

314
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,022
[♪ eerie music plays]

315
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:07,235
[eerie laughter]

316
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:11,656
I'm sure it's some kind of vengeful ghost.

317
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:14,742
It's asking us to catch the killer.

318
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:17,995
How will you take care of this?

319
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:20,331
I'll check it out first.

320
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:22,667
Mmm. To arrest a ghost?

321
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:24,835
Or perform an exorcism?

322
00:17:26,128 --> 00:17:28,047
What if there's actually
something there, huh?

323
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,966
You can't just brush off a tip, damn it.

324
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:33,386
By the way,
you're straight-up talking down to me now.

325
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:35,012
I mean, well,

326
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:37,932
we're the same rank now,

327
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,767
and the same age.

328
00:17:39,850 --> 00:17:42,186
And you're not my instructor anymore.

329
00:17:43,646 --> 00:17:46,482
Do what you want.
Who am I to stop a nutjob?

330
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,571
-Let's head over there.
-What?

331
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:52,947
Let's go check it out.

332
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,824
[♪ upbeat music playing]

333
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:56,450
Aren't you clocking out?

334
00:17:56,534 --> 00:17:57,952
I've got nothing to do at home.

335
00:17:58,578 --> 00:18:00,037
Forget it. I'm going alone.

336
00:18:00,121 --> 00:18:01,205
I should come with you.

337
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,125
What if a ghost latches onto you?

338
00:18:04,959 --> 00:18:06,377
[chuckles] Come on.

339
00:18:10,715 --> 00:18:12,091
[♪ quirky music playing]

340
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:16,429
Let's take your car.

341
00:18:17,305 --> 00:18:18,723
Why? What is it this time?

342
00:18:19,307 --> 00:18:21,726
Then we can take my bike
and you hang on to my waist.

343
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:23,352
No, we can just go separately.

344
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:27,231
Come on, don't be so heartless.

345
00:18:27,315 --> 00:18:29,108
I want to ride in a car like this, too.

346
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,943
Open the door.

347
00:18:31,861 --> 00:18:32,987
[sighs]

348
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:34,989
[car alarm chirping]

349
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,326
[clicks tongue]

350
00:18:42,163 --> 00:18:43,331
Ooh.

351
00:18:43,414 --> 00:18:44,749
Nice car.

352
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,378
Off we go.

353
00:18:49,462 --> 00:18:50,963
[engine starts]

354
00:18:59,096 --> 00:19:00,348
[tires screech]

355
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:13,569
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

356
00:19:13,653 --> 00:19:15,988
FOR SALE

357
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:17,990
[gate creaking]

358
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:22,912
[Isoo shudders]

359
00:19:23,913 --> 00:19:25,039
It's eerie.

360
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,249
Is this a haunted house or something?

361
00:19:29,627 --> 00:19:30,628
[Ahin gasps] Oh, my God.

362
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:32,755
They actually came.

363
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,674
[Ahin's mother] Ahin, come out for dinner.

364
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:35,758
I'm not eating.

365
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:43,766
[Isoo exhales softly]

366
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,820
[Hyera] The body was here.

367
00:19:56,487 --> 00:19:58,197
Do you know what kind of case it was?

368
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:00,282
No.

369
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:03,411
-[muffled clattering]
-[glass shattering]

370
00:20:03,494 --> 00:20:05,329
-[muffled screaming]
-[Hyera] There was a struggle,

371
00:20:06,372 --> 00:20:08,290
and they resisted until the end,

372
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:12,253
but were eventually killed
and became ghosts?

373
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,423
You believe that?

374
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:17,842
-Ghosts and stuff?
-No.

375
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:20,720
I would if I saw one, but I never have.

376
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:23,055
I like horror movies, though. You?

377
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:25,224
I don't watch that stuff.

378
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:27,101
[chuckles softly]

379
00:20:27,184 --> 00:20:28,352
So you get scared easily.

380
00:20:28,978 --> 00:20:30,396
Of course not.

381
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:32,314
I just find them boring, that's all.

382
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,691
Why bother watching that?

383
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,282
[yelps]

384
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:44,577
-[chuckles]
-Oh, come on!

385
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:46,203
Really boring, isn't it?

386
00:20:46,287 --> 00:20:47,455
-[chuckles]
-[exhales deeply]

387
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:49,582
[exhales]

388
00:20:49,999 --> 00:20:51,292
You check upstairs.

389
00:20:53,169 --> 00:20:54,420
I'll check this side.

390
00:20:55,171 --> 00:20:56,380
[sighs]

391
00:20:56,464 --> 00:20:58,340
[muttering] She's seriously annoying.

392
00:21:00,176 --> 00:21:02,261
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

393
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,518
[exhales deeply]

394
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:22,823
Oh!

395
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,326
[door creaking]

396
00:21:48,516 --> 00:21:49,767
[animal squeaking]

397
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:50,976
[yelps]

398
00:21:54,188 --> 00:21:55,272
[exhales sharply]

399
00:22:01,237 --> 00:22:02,738
[♪ ominous music swells, fades]

400
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:03,823
[blunt thud]

401
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:05,449
[panting]

402
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:16,877
[door creaking]

403
00:22:20,714 --> 00:22:21,715
Meow.

404
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:23,092
[♪ ominous music swells, fades]

405
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:24,510
-[blunt thud]
-[heavy fall]

406
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:27,429
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

407
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:30,975
-[Ahin's mother] Park Ahin.
-[Ahin] I said I'm not eating.

408
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:33,143
Don't you dare make noodles
at midnight again.

409
00:22:33,227 --> 00:22:35,062
Okay, fine. I'm busy.

410
00:22:35,563 --> 00:22:38,065
-What on earth are you watching with--
-Please just...

411
00:22:40,526 --> 00:22:42,194
Good luck making it to the academy.

412
00:22:42,278 --> 00:22:44,572
Just get out.

413
00:22:44,655 --> 00:22:45,906
-[Ahin's mother] Goodness, what are you...
-[door opens]

414
00:22:45,990 --> 00:22:47,074
Park Ahin!

415
00:22:57,585 --> 00:22:58,794
[Hyera coughing]

416
00:22:58,878 --> 00:22:59,962
[♪ tense music playing]

417
00:23:00,045 --> 00:23:01,505
[groaning]

418
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:04,174
[panting]

419
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,885
[grunts]

420
00:23:08,053 --> 00:23:09,263
Detective Jin.

421
00:23:09,972 --> 00:23:11,140
Jin Isoo!

422
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,725
Nutjob!

423
00:23:13,392 --> 00:23:15,144
Yes, ma'am!

424
00:23:16,395 --> 00:23:17,438
[Hyera grunts]

425
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:19,356
-What's this?
-Jin Isoo.

426
00:23:20,399 --> 00:23:21,400
Snap out of it.

427
00:23:22,276 --> 00:23:23,736
I'm completely awake.

428
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:25,195
What's going on?

429
00:23:25,279 --> 00:23:27,281
-Hey, what happened?
-I don't know.

430
00:23:27,781 --> 00:23:29,325
I got attacked out of nowhere.

431
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:30,993
-[panting]
-[Isoo grunts]

432
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:34,955
[groans]

433
00:23:48,886 --> 00:23:49,887
[grunts]

434
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,972
[panting] Hey, try to untie this.

435
00:23:52,056 --> 00:23:53,265
[in English] Okay.

436
00:23:53,349 --> 00:23:55,225
[in Korean] I actually have
pretty long fingers.

437
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:57,311
[grunts]

438
00:23:57,394 --> 00:23:58,646
I got it.

439
00:23:58,729 --> 00:24:00,230
-That's my finger.
-Oh.

440
00:24:00,314 --> 00:24:01,357
Thought it was a rope.

441
00:24:02,024 --> 00:24:03,817
Stop messing around. We could die here.

442
00:24:03,901 --> 00:24:05,319
No one's going to die.

443
00:24:05,402 --> 00:24:06,820
Why are you being so dramatic?

444
00:24:06,904 --> 00:24:09,031
We don't know who attacked us.

445
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,741
Okay, fine.

446
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:12,076
Just stay still, will you?

447
00:24:14,787 --> 00:24:16,372
[grunts, exhales]

448
00:24:18,374 --> 00:24:19,416
[gasps]

449
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:20,834
What is it?

450
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:24,964
Nothing. It's nothing.

451
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:28,050
No need to be alarmed. Stay calm.

452
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,301
-Stay calm.
-[screams]

453
00:24:29,385 --> 00:24:31,387
Why is this being so difficult?

454
00:24:32,429 --> 00:24:33,764
[grunting]

455
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:35,724
[sniffs]

456
00:24:35,808 --> 00:24:37,768
Hey, I smell something burning.

457
00:24:38,352 --> 00:24:39,353
She's got a good nose.

458
00:24:39,979 --> 00:24:41,897
[exhales] Is there a fire?

459
00:24:41,981 --> 00:24:44,650
Kind of. No, it's fine.
We're okay for now.

460
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:47,111
[grunts]

461
00:24:50,364 --> 00:24:51,365
Hey, Jin Isoo.

462
00:24:51,448 --> 00:24:53,283
I'm working on it! Jeez.

463
00:24:53,367 --> 00:24:55,828
Do you see that broken glass over there?

464
00:24:56,537 --> 00:24:57,830
Yeah.

465
00:24:57,913 --> 00:24:59,039
On three, fall left.

466
00:24:59,123 --> 00:25:00,374
Left? Okay.

467
00:25:00,457 --> 00:25:02,584
One, two,

468
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:03,752
three.

469
00:25:03,836 --> 00:25:05,129
[both groan]

470
00:25:06,630 --> 00:25:08,048
[breathing heavily]

471
00:25:08,132 --> 00:25:09,383
It was my right.

472
00:25:10,092 --> 00:25:12,177
-[breathing heavily]
-You need to be more specific.

473
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:15,597
Again. One...

474
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:17,224
-Two, three!
-Two, three!

475
00:25:18,142 --> 00:25:19,435
[both groaning, grunting]

476
00:25:22,688 --> 00:25:23,689
[Hyera] Get up.

477
00:25:24,314 --> 00:25:26,150
-Get up.
-One, two, three.

478
00:25:26,859 --> 00:25:27,901
[grunts]

479
00:25:28,485 --> 00:25:30,779
Again. One, two, three.

480
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:32,656
[both grunting]

481
00:25:34,408 --> 00:25:36,160
-Where is it?
-Go up.

482
00:25:37,411 --> 00:25:38,746
A bit farther.

483
00:25:39,872 --> 00:25:41,165
[both grunting]

484
00:25:41,915 --> 00:25:42,916
Got it.

485
00:25:44,376 --> 00:25:45,627
Be careful.

486
00:25:45,711 --> 00:25:47,087
Don't move. You'll get hurt.

487
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:50,174
[mutters]

488
00:25:51,884 --> 00:25:53,052
[Hyera grunting]

489
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:07,816
[♪ ominous music plays]

490
00:26:10,861 --> 00:26:12,321
Fire. [breath trembles]

491
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:14,323
It's a fire. [breathing heavily]

492
00:26:15,574 --> 00:26:16,950
[landline ringing]

493
00:26:18,285 --> 00:26:19,870
Yes, this is Violent Crime Team 1.

494
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:22,081
There's a fire.

495
00:26:22,164 --> 00:26:24,541
The detectives went inside,
but now it's on fire.

496
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:27,544
[♪ foreboding music playing]

497
00:26:27,628 --> 00:26:29,046
[Isoo grunting]

498
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:32,007
[grunts]

499
00:26:32,091 --> 00:26:33,634
[both panting]

500
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,182
[Isoo groaning]

501
00:26:41,350 --> 00:26:42,601
[grunting]

502
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:47,731
-[rope snaps]
-[grunts]

503
00:26:47,815 --> 00:26:48,941
[sighs in relief]

504
00:26:49,024 --> 00:26:50,025
[grunting]

505
00:26:50,567 --> 00:26:51,819
-[rope snaps]
-[exhales]

506
00:26:52,486 --> 00:26:53,779
[both panting]

507
00:26:58,158 --> 00:26:59,243
How do we get out?

508
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:01,787
[rattling]

509
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:06,083
Like this.

510
00:27:06,708 --> 00:27:07,960
Get out of the way.

511
00:27:11,004 --> 00:27:12,297
[glass shattering]

512
00:27:15,175 --> 00:27:16,426
[clanging]

513
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:24,101
[in English] Ladies first.

514
00:27:24,184 --> 00:27:25,185
[exhales heavily]

515
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:30,858
[both coughing]

516
00:27:30,941 --> 00:27:32,192
[breathing heavily]

517
00:27:32,276 --> 00:27:33,277
[exclaims]

518
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,112
[in Korean] If it weren't for me,

519
00:27:35,195 --> 00:27:37,364
you would've burned to death
in that house.

520
00:27:37,447 --> 00:27:38,907
It would've been the end.

521
00:27:39,950 --> 00:27:42,452
Detective Joo,
just stay close to me from now on.

522
00:27:42,536 --> 00:27:45,289
The hero never dies that easily.

523
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:46,498
You want to live?

524
00:27:46,582 --> 00:27:49,001
Then just stick close to me, okay?

525
00:27:49,084 --> 00:27:50,085
Okay.

526
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:53,463
[sighs] What do we do now?

527
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:55,924
Do we jump, or not?

528
00:27:58,051 --> 00:27:59,636
-Like this?
-What?

529
00:28:00,721 --> 00:28:02,431
-[Isoo gasps]
-[explosion]

530
00:28:11,648 --> 00:28:13,066
[both groan]

531
00:28:13,150 --> 00:28:14,568
[both panting]

532
00:28:17,863 --> 00:28:19,281
Nutjob, you okay?

533
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:22,075
Yeah. I seriously almost died.

534
00:28:22,576 --> 00:28:24,411
[grunts, groans]

535
00:28:24,995 --> 00:28:28,040
You should've told me we were jumping.
Look how high that is.

536
00:28:28,123 --> 00:28:29,917
-[groans]
-[exhales heavily]

537
00:28:30,584 --> 00:28:32,294
The hero never dies that easily.

538
00:28:32,961 --> 00:28:34,838
Stay close to me if you want to live.

539
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:37,007
[scoffs]

540
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:40,260
[grunts]

541
00:28:40,344 --> 00:28:41,637
[both continue panting]

542
00:28:44,473 --> 00:28:46,141
There really is something here.

543
00:28:46,808 --> 00:28:49,353
[sighs] I have great instincts, huh?

544
00:28:50,312 --> 00:28:51,730
[scoffs]

545
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:54,274
Oh, you're bleeding.

546
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:56,818
I'm fine.

547
00:28:56,902 --> 00:28:58,654
Come on.

548
00:28:59,988 --> 00:29:00,989
Give it here.

549
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:09,081
-Aah!
-You said you were fine.

550
00:29:09,164 --> 00:29:11,041
You're tying it too tight, so it hurts.

551
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:14,002
It's to stop the bleeding. [clicks tongue]

552
00:29:14,086 --> 00:29:15,671
You shouldn't have gone overboard.

553
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:17,130
That's my thing.

554
00:29:18,632 --> 00:29:19,841
[Isoo sighs]

555
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:21,176
-[gate clunks open]
-[Kyungjin] Jin Isoo!

556
00:29:24,262 --> 00:29:25,931
-Bro!
-[Junyoung] There they are again.

557
00:29:26,014 --> 00:29:27,140
Are you okay?

558
00:29:27,224 --> 00:29:28,725
I'm not, but don't make a fuss.

559
00:29:29,393 --> 00:29:30,686
Are you okay, Detective Joo?

560
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:32,813
Yes.

561
00:29:32,896 --> 00:29:34,356
What happened?

562
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:35,440
It was arson.

563
00:29:35,941 --> 00:29:37,526
Someone tied us up and set a fire.

564
00:29:38,235 --> 00:29:39,319
[exhales heavily]

565
00:29:40,696 --> 00:29:41,738
[exhales heavily]

566
00:29:42,239 --> 00:29:43,865
[leaves rustling]

567
00:29:45,409 --> 00:29:46,785
[Ahin] Detective!

568
00:29:46,868 --> 00:29:47,911
[panting shakily]

569
00:29:47,995 --> 00:29:49,079
-[whimpers]
-Oh.

570
00:29:52,249 --> 00:29:53,291
[mouthing]

571
00:29:53,375 --> 00:29:54,459
Who is this?

572
00:29:54,543 --> 00:29:58,547
[whimpers] I'm so sorry. I didn't see
anything because I was eating noodles.

573
00:29:59,965 --> 00:30:02,342
Ah, you must be Ahin.

574
00:30:03,677 --> 00:30:05,929
Are you okay?

575
00:30:06,513 --> 00:30:07,723
Huh?

576
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:10,642
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

577
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:14,855
Have we met somewhere before?

578
00:30:14,938 --> 00:30:16,523
[♪ ominous music playing]

579
00:30:17,858 --> 00:30:19,359
[sirens blaring]

580
00:30:33,623 --> 00:30:36,043
-Take a video of the onlookers.
-Yes, ma'am.

581
00:30:46,053 --> 00:30:48,013
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

582
00:30:48,096 --> 00:30:49,639
[indistinct chatter]

583
00:30:54,436 --> 00:30:57,022
How did you end up here?

584
00:30:57,105 --> 00:30:58,315
We got a report.

585
00:30:58,398 --> 00:30:59,775
What kind of report?

586
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:03,403
That middle schooler reported that
someone keeps entering an empty house.

587
00:31:04,696 --> 00:31:06,156
We came to check just in case.

588
00:31:06,239 --> 00:31:07,657
Did you see who attacked you?

589
00:31:08,992 --> 00:31:10,202
They came up from behind.

590
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:12,079
Without knowing who you were?

591
00:31:12,662 --> 00:31:13,663
Yeah.

592
00:31:15,457 --> 00:31:17,709
It's not some punk
squatting in an empty house.

593
00:31:19,419 --> 00:31:20,879
There's something going on here.

594
00:31:31,431 --> 00:31:33,100
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

595
00:31:52,828 --> 00:31:53,912
What is this?

596
00:31:56,623 --> 00:31:58,250
Guys, come here. Quickly.

597
00:32:04,965 --> 00:32:07,092
Let's open it up.

598
00:32:07,175 --> 00:32:10,011
The padlock is too new
for a long-abandoned house.

599
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:12,722
Look. Someone tried to pry it open.

600
00:32:12,806 --> 00:32:14,474
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

601
00:32:16,893 --> 00:32:17,894
That?

602
00:32:17,978 --> 00:32:19,729
There's definitely something in there.

603
00:32:20,397 --> 00:32:21,731
Some kind of dark secret.

604
00:32:21,815 --> 00:32:23,066
[distant cameras clicking]

605
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:28,155
I told you, I've got great instincts.

606
00:32:28,238 --> 00:32:29,281
You two know that.

607
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:31,408
Get a search warrant.

608
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:33,618
Why would we need a warrant?
We almost died.

609
00:32:33,702 --> 00:32:34,911
That's not enough.

610
00:32:39,374 --> 00:32:40,625
We'll say it was on fire.

611
00:32:40,709 --> 00:32:41,918
We can't.

612
00:32:42,586 --> 00:32:43,587
Kyungjin.

613
00:32:46,590 --> 00:32:47,591
We can't.

614
00:32:48,175 --> 00:32:49,217
[mutters]

615
00:32:51,887 --> 00:32:53,346
-[Junyoung sighs]
-[mutters]

616
00:32:53,430 --> 00:32:54,431
Hey, come on.

617
00:32:55,348 --> 00:32:58,268
If you open it now, whatever we find
inside will be inadmissible.

618
00:32:58,351 --> 00:32:59,352
You know the drill.

619
00:33:00,187 --> 00:33:01,188
But...

620
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:03,857
-[crowbar clinks softly]
-By the way,

621
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:07,319
why do you keep
talking casually to our team leader?

622
00:33:08,486 --> 00:33:11,364
I told her I'd be respectful,
but she kept telling me to relax.

623
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,283
Goodness.

624
00:33:13,366 --> 00:33:14,701
She's super chill.

625
00:33:14,784 --> 00:33:15,952
Honestly.

626
00:33:17,746 --> 00:33:19,706
Don't open it. Don't you dare.

627
00:33:21,041 --> 00:33:22,209
[footsteps receding]

628
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:29,257
[sighs wearily]

629
00:33:29,341 --> 00:33:31,468
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

630
00:33:32,427 --> 00:33:33,511
[Isoo exhales deeply]

631
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:39,893
[softly] Ah...

632
00:33:41,645 --> 00:33:42,854
[cell phone vibrating]

633
00:33:46,107 --> 00:33:48,235
Detective Joo, are you okay? Are you hurt?

634
00:33:48,318 --> 00:33:49,819
No, I'm fine, sir.

635
00:33:50,779 --> 00:33:51,863
[sighs in relief]

636
00:33:52,530 --> 00:33:53,531
What happened?

637
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:56,493
We don't know yet.

638
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:59,204
I think we need to do
some more digging on this house.

639
00:33:59,955 --> 00:34:03,500
Okay. I've sent the forensics team,
so wrap it up and go home.

640
00:34:03,583 --> 00:34:04,960
Sir.

641
00:34:06,628 --> 00:34:08,630
We found a suspicious basement here.

642
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:10,382
But it's locked with a padlock.

643
00:34:11,132 --> 00:34:12,592
Can we get a warrant?

644
00:34:12,676 --> 00:34:15,929
We need to know what kind of case this is
to request a warrant.

645
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:18,682
Why? You think
it has something to do with the fire?

646
00:34:18,765 --> 00:34:20,475
I'm not sure.

647
00:34:21,476 --> 00:34:22,644
In that case,

648
00:34:22,727 --> 00:34:25,188
investigate first,
then get a warrant if you need to.

649
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:27,607
Yes, sir.

650
00:34:32,654 --> 00:34:35,240
-We'll have to see about the warrant.
-Okay.

651
00:34:40,120 --> 00:34:42,330
The fire started on the first floor,

652
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:45,083
then appears to have spread up the stairs.

653
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:47,460
I heard there was
a murder here a long time ago,

654
00:34:47,544 --> 00:34:49,754
but someone's been in and out since then.

655
00:34:49,838 --> 00:34:52,132
Okay. We'll look for any recent traces.

656
00:34:54,301 --> 00:34:57,095
We'll go collect security footage
from the streets nearby.

657
00:34:57,178 --> 00:34:58,179
Okay.

658
00:34:58,263 --> 00:34:59,723
-Let's go.
-Okay.

659
00:34:59,806 --> 00:35:01,850
[distant metal clanging]

660
00:35:07,063 --> 00:35:08,148
[grunts]

661
00:35:10,525 --> 00:35:11,526
-[Hyera] Jin Isoo!
-[Junyoung] Hey!

662
00:35:14,029 --> 00:35:15,905
-What are you doing?
-I told you not to.

663
00:35:15,989 --> 00:35:17,073
[chain rattling]

664
00:35:18,742 --> 00:35:19,784
Hey!

665
00:35:20,827 --> 00:35:24,581
Is it illegal for a homeowner
to break down his own door?

666
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:26,082
No way.

667
00:35:26,958 --> 00:35:28,209
I bought this house.

668
00:35:28,293 --> 00:35:30,337
-[chuckles softly]
-You bought it?

669
00:35:30,420 --> 00:35:32,589
The realtor's number
was on the front gate.

670
00:35:32,672 --> 00:35:33,715
FOR SALE

671
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,133
[♪ jaunty music playing]

672
00:35:35,216 --> 00:35:37,427
The owner asked them
to sell it no matter what.

673
00:35:37,510 --> 00:35:40,013
[scoffs] So you just bought it?

674
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:41,097
[Kyungjin] Wow, bro.

675
00:35:41,181 --> 00:35:42,349
[clapping]

676
00:35:42,432 --> 00:35:44,100
Who just spends money like that...

677
00:35:45,435 --> 00:35:47,604
except you, of course.

678
00:35:47,687 --> 00:35:48,688
You know how to flex.

679
00:35:48,772 --> 00:35:49,814
Mmm.

680
00:35:49,898 --> 00:35:52,192
[sighs] So this is your cheat code.

681
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:54,694
This is nothing to be surprised about.

682
00:35:54,778 --> 00:35:56,071
You're pretty timid.

683
00:35:57,364 --> 00:35:58,990
Where did you get that hammer?

684
00:35:59,074 --> 00:36:01,701
I borrowed it from Ahin.
They're repairing their wall.

685
00:36:01,785 --> 00:36:03,536
-All right, then.
-[chain rattling]

686
00:36:05,747 --> 00:36:08,333
Now, don't be shy.

687
00:36:08,917 --> 00:36:10,585
-[chain clatters]
-[in English] Welcome.

688
00:36:10,669 --> 00:36:12,170
[door creaking]

689
00:36:16,716 --> 00:36:18,593
[♪ eerie music playing]

690
00:36:26,476 --> 00:36:27,686
[Kyungjin coughing]

691
00:36:42,867 --> 00:36:43,868
[Kyungjin clears throat]

692
00:36:47,580 --> 00:36:48,581
[in Korean] Detective Joo.

693
00:36:49,958 --> 00:36:51,126
That looks newly covered.

694
00:36:57,090 --> 00:36:58,216
[hollow thudding]

695
00:37:03,138 --> 00:37:04,139
Kyungjin.

696
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:16,776
Stand back.

697
00:37:24,117 --> 00:37:25,201
[sharp clang]

698
00:37:34,294 --> 00:37:35,462
[sharp clang]

699
00:37:36,546 --> 00:37:37,547
Detective Joo.

700
00:37:38,339 --> 00:37:39,424
[scraping]

701
00:37:42,802 --> 00:37:45,096
[stones clattering]

702
00:38:03,990 --> 00:38:05,325
[exhales deeply]

703
00:38:05,408 --> 00:38:07,535
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

704
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:20,632
[Junyoung grunting]

705
00:38:31,726 --> 00:38:32,811
[exclaims]

706
00:38:33,603 --> 00:38:35,522
[Isoo coughs, gags]

707
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:49,285
GANGHA 3-DONG
BURIED BODIES CASE

708
00:38:50,912 --> 00:38:52,205
[exhales]

709
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:55,083
How did you end up going to that house?

710
00:38:55,583 --> 00:38:57,502
[Isoo] We received a tip.

711
00:38:59,254 --> 00:39:00,505
What kind of tip?

712
00:39:01,965 --> 00:39:04,008
Someone reported that there was a ghost.

713
00:39:04,634 --> 00:39:05,677
To me.

714
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:07,053
[♪ jaunty music playing]

715
00:39:09,097 --> 00:39:11,766
Hey, what is he talking about?
Did he just say a ghost?

716
00:39:11,850 --> 00:39:14,811
[chuckles softly] It was a report
of lights in an empty house.

717
00:39:15,353 --> 00:39:18,648
We went to check if it was being used
for criminal activity.

718
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,441
Okay, fine.

719
00:39:21,442 --> 00:39:23,570
Why did you open the basement?
I said wait.

720
00:39:23,653 --> 00:39:25,488
I went ahead and bought the house!

721
00:39:28,616 --> 00:39:29,617
I see.

722
00:39:30,285 --> 00:39:31,411
You bought the house.

723
00:39:33,162 --> 00:39:34,831
[chuckles, exhales]

724
00:39:37,834 --> 00:39:38,877
Right, so,

725
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:41,671
you uncovered five bodies?

726
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:43,798
Yes, they're performing the autopsy now.

727
00:39:43,882 --> 00:39:45,174
ONE BODY, BURIED RECENTLY

728
00:39:45,258 --> 00:39:48,469
Four of them are skeletal remains,
so identifying them will take a while.

729
00:39:48,553 --> 00:39:49,679
[Changun sighs]

730
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:51,639
For now,

731
00:39:51,723 --> 00:39:53,558
Team 1 and 2 will both be on this case.

732
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:55,685
Make sure this doesn't leak to the press,

733
00:39:55,768 --> 00:39:57,937
and identify the victims quickly. Got it?

734
00:39:58,021 --> 00:39:59,439
-Yes, sir.
-[all] Yes, sir.

735
00:40:00,899 --> 00:40:02,984
[inhales deeply, exhales]

736
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:10,575
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

737
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:17,582
[examiner] Let's begin the autopsy.

738
00:40:40,980 --> 00:40:42,482
[camera shutter clicking]

739
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:03,628
I investigated the murder
that happened inside the house.

740
00:41:04,629 --> 00:41:07,840
Around 1:00 a.m. on October 25, 2016,

741
00:41:07,924 --> 00:41:11,469
a couple and their son, a college student,
were all murdered.

742
00:41:13,596 --> 00:41:15,640
There were no signs of forced entry,

743
00:41:16,307 --> 00:41:17,934
but cash and jewelry were gone,

744
00:41:18,017 --> 00:41:20,645
so it was suspected to be
a robbery-homicide,

745
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:22,730
but the culprit was never caught.

746
00:41:22,814 --> 00:41:24,273
It's a cold case.

747
00:41:25,233 --> 00:41:26,818
No fingerprints, no hair.

748
00:41:26,901 --> 00:41:28,820
Not a single trace was left behind.

749
00:41:28,903 --> 00:41:32,907
So the house was abandoned after that,
and then it was used as a burial site.

750
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:35,201
By the serial killer.

751
00:41:36,995 --> 00:41:38,079
[Byungsik sighs]

752
00:41:39,789 --> 00:41:40,790
Detective Joo.

753
00:41:42,375 --> 00:41:44,877
The most recently deceased victim

754
00:41:44,961 --> 00:41:46,462
had these glasses in their pants.

755
00:41:49,799 --> 00:41:51,634
[Byungsik] I'll go check it out.

756
00:41:52,218 --> 00:41:53,886
Okay. We'll go after the arsonist.

757
00:41:53,970 --> 00:41:55,304
Got it. Let's go.

758
00:41:55,388 --> 00:41:56,389
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

759
00:41:58,141 --> 00:42:00,977
-Let's check the footage from the scene.
-Okay.

760
00:42:03,813 --> 00:42:04,814
[mouse clicks]

761
00:42:07,108 --> 00:42:09,277
[♪ gripping music playing]

762
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:15,533
-[in English] Stop.
-[keyboard key clacks]

763
00:42:16,826 --> 00:42:18,786
[in Korean] That's the guy.
The black hoodie.

764
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:20,371
-Track him.
-Okay.

765
00:42:20,455 --> 00:42:21,581
[keyboard clacking]

766
00:42:40,141 --> 00:42:41,184
It's a rental.

767
00:42:41,267 --> 00:42:42,643
-Run the plate.
-Got it.

768
00:42:49,817 --> 00:42:50,818
Excuse me.

769
00:42:52,445 --> 00:42:53,446
We're with the police.

770
00:42:53,529 --> 00:42:54,614
How can I help you?

771
00:42:54,697 --> 00:42:56,365
Could you tell us

772
00:42:56,449 --> 00:42:59,327
where you supplied these glasses?

773
00:42:59,410 --> 00:43:00,953
I'll check right away.

774
00:43:06,918 --> 00:43:07,919
DOHYUN CAR RENTAL

775
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:10,088
[♪ gripping music continues]

776
00:43:10,171 --> 00:43:12,006
Who rented this car?

777
00:43:12,840 --> 00:43:15,259
[agent] Oh, that car
hasn't been returned yet.

778
00:43:15,718 --> 00:43:16,719
One moment, please.

779
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:24,018
Oh...

780
00:43:25,645 --> 00:43:26,646
It's that car there.

781
00:43:28,981 --> 00:43:29,982
Right.

782
00:43:30,441 --> 00:43:31,442
[door chimes]

783
00:43:32,902 --> 00:43:34,112
Hey, hey.

784
00:43:40,118 --> 00:43:41,119
Police.

785
00:43:41,202 --> 00:43:43,579
-[knocks window]
-Please come out, serial killer.

786
00:43:43,663 --> 00:43:44,956
Careful. He could be armed.

787
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:46,290
You're right.

788
00:43:47,667 --> 00:43:48,668
[knocks window]

789
00:43:48,751 --> 00:43:49,877
Come out.

790
00:43:49,961 --> 00:43:51,170
Or we'll break it.

791
00:43:59,929 --> 00:44:01,347
[window whirring]

792
00:44:15,069 --> 00:44:18,114
JEONG DAEUN
GANGHA 3-DONG ARSON SUSPECT

793
00:44:22,076 --> 00:44:23,828
[Isoo breathes sharply]

794
00:44:23,911 --> 00:44:25,037
[inhales sharply]

795
00:44:25,121 --> 00:44:26,747
Inside that abandoned house,

796
00:44:28,457 --> 00:44:29,500
did you attack us?

797
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:31,210
What?

798
00:44:31,294 --> 00:44:33,462
Did you knock us out and tie us up?

799
00:44:33,546 --> 00:44:36,340
No, how would I even do that?

800
00:44:36,424 --> 00:44:39,051
Last night, you were
at the abandoned house

801
00:44:39,135 --> 00:44:40,469
at 14-1 Gangha 3-dong, right?

802
00:44:41,846 --> 00:44:42,847
Yes.

803
00:44:45,141 --> 00:44:47,560
I started the fire.

804
00:44:47,643 --> 00:44:48,644
[exhales in disbelief]

805
00:44:49,020 --> 00:44:50,605
We almost burned to death.

806
00:44:50,688 --> 00:44:52,440
My team leader hurt her arm.

807
00:44:52,523 --> 00:44:55,610
I'm really sorry.
I didn't know there were people inside.

808
00:44:56,944 --> 00:44:58,529
Why did you start the fire?

809
00:44:59,572 --> 00:45:01,616
Because Hyeonsu disappeared,

810
00:45:03,201 --> 00:45:05,328
and no one will believe me.

811
00:45:07,038 --> 00:45:08,789
Please start from the beginning.

812
00:45:10,499 --> 00:45:13,002
Hyeonsu is a lawyer.

813
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:14,545
[♪ soft suspenseful music playing]

814
00:45:14,629 --> 00:45:16,297
We've been dating for three years,

815
00:45:17,465 --> 00:45:19,342
and we were about to get married.

816
00:45:20,843 --> 00:45:21,969
[vocalizing the "Bridal Chorus"]

817
00:45:22,053 --> 00:45:23,095
4 MONTHS AGO

818
00:45:23,179 --> 00:45:24,639
[both chuckle]

819
00:45:24,722 --> 00:45:26,974
JEONG DAEUN'S FIANCÉ
PARK HYEONSU

820
00:45:27,058 --> 00:45:28,601
[both vocalizing the "Bridal Chorus"]

821
00:45:29,644 --> 00:45:31,229
-[exclaims] It's raining.
-Hold on.

822
00:45:31,312 --> 00:45:32,813
-What?
-It's raining so suddenly.

823
00:45:32,897 --> 00:45:34,941
-[both giggle]
-[Hyeonsu] Let's go.

824
00:45:35,733 --> 00:45:37,318
[♪ melancholy music playing]

825
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:39,528
[Daeun] He was a really kind person.

826
00:45:42,990 --> 00:45:45,409
When we were busy planning our wedding,

827
00:45:45,493 --> 00:45:47,578
he said something important had come up.

828
00:45:48,204 --> 00:45:50,915
His former classmate was in trouble
and needed his help.

829
00:45:51,540 --> 00:45:53,834
Not long after, she was murdered.

830
00:45:54,543 --> 00:45:55,920
But then I was told

831
00:45:56,462 --> 00:45:58,339
that Hyeonsu was the killer.

832
00:45:58,422 --> 00:46:00,883
I kept saying
he'd never do something like that,

833
00:46:00,967 --> 00:46:02,551
but no one would believe me.

834
00:46:04,095 --> 00:46:05,805
They said all the evidence was there,

835
00:46:05,888 --> 00:46:08,724
that she and Hyeonsu used to date,

836
00:46:09,267 --> 00:46:12,144
that he stalked her to get back with her,
then killed her.

837
00:46:12,895 --> 00:46:14,480
But that doesn't make any sense.

838
00:46:16,315 --> 00:46:17,316
Sir.

839
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:18,609
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

840
00:46:18,693 --> 00:46:19,694
What is it?

841
00:46:27,368 --> 00:46:29,287
PARK HYEONSU

842
00:46:37,003 --> 00:46:38,129
[exhales softly]

843
00:46:38,754 --> 00:46:40,506
Then why did you go to that house?

844
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:51,350
Hyeonsu installed
a location-sharing app on my phone.

845
00:46:51,434 --> 00:46:52,560
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

846
00:46:53,644 --> 00:46:56,188
This app will show you where I am.

847
00:46:56,605 --> 00:46:57,606
[chuckles]

848
00:46:58,524 --> 00:46:59,650
[gasps softly]

849
00:46:59,734 --> 00:47:01,360
We can't see each other very often.

850
00:47:02,111 --> 00:47:05,740
Now, if you just check the app,
you'll know where I'm working.

851
00:47:06,449 --> 00:47:07,742
Oh, you.

852
00:47:07,825 --> 00:47:09,201
[both chuckle]

853
00:47:09,952 --> 00:47:11,287
[Daeun] On the day of the murder,

854
00:47:11,370 --> 00:47:14,832
Hyeonsu's last location was that house.

855
00:47:14,915 --> 00:47:18,377
At first, I was too shaken
and forgot all about the app.

856
00:47:19,045 --> 00:47:21,380
When I later checked
and went to his last location,

857
00:47:21,464 --> 00:47:22,590
it was an abandoned house.

858
00:47:23,382 --> 00:47:25,926
Hyeonsu has no connection
to that neighborhood.

859
00:47:27,386 --> 00:47:28,387
Wait, so,

860
00:47:29,180 --> 00:47:30,806
you went in there alone?

861
00:47:32,224 --> 00:47:33,225
Weren't you scared?

862
00:47:33,309 --> 00:47:35,186
I asked the police to investigate,

863
00:47:35,269 --> 00:47:37,855
but the detective in charge
wouldn't listen.

864
00:47:38,606 --> 00:47:40,524
[♪ gripping music playing]

865
00:47:43,652 --> 00:47:46,864
But there was a strange basement there.

866
00:47:51,369 --> 00:47:52,953
I tried to open it...

867
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:02,296
...but I couldn't.

868
00:48:03,130 --> 00:48:04,382
So I set the place on fire,

869
00:48:06,217 --> 00:48:08,886
thinking they might find something
while putting it out.

870
00:48:10,262 --> 00:48:12,681
I honestly didn't know someone was inside.

871
00:48:14,308 --> 00:48:15,434
By any chance,

872
00:48:16,268 --> 00:48:18,020
did you see anyone suspicious there?

873
00:48:19,355 --> 00:48:21,482
No, no one.

874
00:48:22,066 --> 00:48:23,275
[sighs softly]

875
00:48:30,324 --> 00:48:31,367
[pen clicks]

876
00:48:34,954 --> 00:48:35,955
[sighs heavily]

877
00:48:36,539 --> 00:48:37,623
[door opens]

878
00:48:38,874 --> 00:48:39,875
[Junyoung] Jiwon.

879
00:48:39,959 --> 00:48:41,001
[door closes]

880
00:48:41,502 --> 00:48:42,586
[Dr. Yoon] Hi.

881
00:48:43,337 --> 00:48:45,464
Have you eaten at all?

882
00:48:46,173 --> 00:48:47,299
No. [exhales]

883
00:48:47,383 --> 00:48:48,926
I wasn't really hungry.

884
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:51,429
I got you a sandwich.

885
00:48:52,638 --> 00:48:53,639
Thanks.

886
00:48:55,516 --> 00:48:56,725
I'll eat it later.

887
00:49:00,187 --> 00:49:01,230
[sighs]

888
00:49:01,313 --> 00:49:03,441
Did you find anything?

889
00:49:04,233 --> 00:49:05,401
[exhales heavily]

890
00:49:06,318 --> 00:49:08,946
We start work on the skeletal remains
tomorrow morning.

891
00:49:09,530 --> 00:49:12,283
We performed the autopsy
on the most recent victim first...

892
00:49:12,366 --> 00:49:13,409
[inhales deeply]

893
00:49:14,410 --> 00:49:15,870
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

894
00:49:15,953 --> 00:49:18,581
...but the body's too decomposed
to recover any fingerprints.

895
00:49:19,331 --> 00:49:22,042
Look here. There are three stab wounds.

896
00:49:22,626 --> 00:49:26,088
And the wrists have marks
that appear to be from duct tape.

897
00:49:26,172 --> 00:49:29,008
So the victim was stabbed while tied up?

898
00:49:30,593 --> 00:49:31,844
[sighs heavily]

899
00:49:31,927 --> 00:49:32,928
Yes.

900
00:49:38,267 --> 00:49:40,936
DETECTIVE DIVISION

901
00:49:41,020 --> 00:49:42,104
You? Against me?

902
00:49:42,605 --> 00:49:44,273
That's ridiculous.

903
00:49:44,356 --> 00:49:45,357
It's him.

904
00:49:47,318 --> 00:49:49,403
The detective who wouldn't believe me.

905
00:49:58,204 --> 00:50:00,122
Sir, how did this happen?

906
00:50:02,666 --> 00:50:05,002
We didn't make a mistake.

907
00:50:20,768 --> 00:50:21,810
INVESTIGATION REPORT

908
00:50:22,937 --> 00:50:24,730
Three months ago, in Yuseon-dong,

909
00:50:25,481 --> 00:50:26,941
Kim Minseo was murdered.

910
00:50:27,024 --> 00:50:28,901
[♪ foreboding music playing]

911
00:50:30,069 --> 00:50:31,445
-Hello.
-Hello.

912
00:50:33,572 --> 00:50:35,074
-[muffled screaming]
-[flesh squelching]

913
00:50:36,367 --> 00:50:37,368
[groans softly]

914
00:50:39,620 --> 00:50:40,913
[knife clatters]

915
00:50:41,539 --> 00:50:43,082
[Byungsik] The suspect fled
on a motorcycle,

916
00:50:43,165 --> 00:50:45,251
entered Park Hyeonsu's house...

917
00:50:47,628 --> 00:50:48,837
[suspect grunting]

918
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:53,175
...then drove away in his car.

919
00:50:57,846 --> 00:50:59,390
[inhales deeply]

920
00:50:59,473 --> 00:51:00,849
Even so,

921
00:51:01,976 --> 00:51:03,602
would a man about to get married,

922
00:51:03,686 --> 00:51:06,188
who was sharing his location
with his girlfriend,

923
00:51:07,064 --> 00:51:08,774
plan and execute a murder?

924
00:51:09,608 --> 00:51:10,734
It doesn't make sense.

925
00:51:11,277 --> 00:51:12,778
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

926
00:51:14,446 --> 00:51:15,447
What was his motive?

927
00:51:20,077 --> 00:51:22,413
Park Hyeonsu kept texting her,
asking to meet up.

928
00:51:23,581 --> 00:51:24,999
[Hyeonsu] Did you take care of it?

929
00:51:25,082 --> 00:51:27,209
I'll be waiting,
so tell me when you're done.

930
00:51:28,335 --> 00:51:30,337
If you keep this up, I'm not holding back.

931
00:51:30,421 --> 00:51:31,630
Please meet me just once.

932
00:51:31,714 --> 00:51:32,923
You want to see me lose it?

933
00:51:33,007 --> 00:51:34,800
Kim Minseo kept refusing.

934
00:51:35,384 --> 00:51:36,760
Kim Minseo

935
00:51:37,595 --> 00:51:39,847
had filed a stalking complaint before.

936
00:51:39,930 --> 00:51:42,766
Park Hyeonsu's fingerprints were
on a knife found at the scene.

937
00:51:45,102 --> 00:51:48,188
That knife was the knife
missing from Park Hyeonsu's house.

938
00:51:48,272 --> 00:51:51,859
We also found the disguise
he used as a courier inside his house.

939
00:51:52,860 --> 00:51:55,613
We confirmed the weapon,
fingerprints, motive, and movements.

940
00:51:55,696 --> 00:51:58,449
Then he suddenly disappeared,
so we put him on the wanted list.

941
00:52:00,326 --> 00:52:01,327
But...

942
00:52:07,041 --> 00:52:08,751
these belong to Park Hyeonsu.

943
00:52:16,091 --> 00:52:17,217
Got the autopsy results?

944
00:52:18,594 --> 00:52:21,889
They'll do the rest tomorrow,
so this is just the most recent victim's.

945
00:52:21,972 --> 00:52:25,851
A male in his 30s. Died three months ago,
and stabbed to death while bound.

946
00:52:25,934 --> 00:52:27,519
[♪ tense music playing]

947
00:52:39,239 --> 00:52:41,158
Wait, so,

948
00:52:41,992 --> 00:52:45,079
the murder suspect you were after
three months ago

949
00:52:45,162 --> 00:52:48,082
was murdered and his body was found
at the abandoned house?

950
00:52:49,249 --> 00:52:50,751
[Isoo inhales deeply]

951
00:52:50,834 --> 00:52:54,296
Did someone get revenge on him?

952
00:52:55,214 --> 00:52:56,799
Does Kim Minseo have any family?

953
00:52:57,841 --> 00:52:59,426
Her husband and her parents.

954
00:52:59,510 --> 00:53:02,638
How can you find and kill someone
even the police couldn't find?

955
00:53:03,472 --> 00:53:05,891
What about the abandoned house?
Did he even go there?

956
00:53:06,600 --> 00:53:09,645
His phone went offline near there
and never came back online.

957
00:53:09,728 --> 00:53:13,065
His car was found
abandoned at Incheon Port.

958
00:53:13,565 --> 00:53:17,069
We assumed
he'd snuck out of the country by sea,

959
00:53:17,152 --> 00:53:19,780
so we had Interpol issue a Red Notice.

960
00:53:21,073 --> 00:53:22,199
[exhales deeply]

961
00:53:30,124 --> 00:53:31,750
Let's verify this first.

962
00:53:32,668 --> 00:53:36,213
Ask them to compare
the body's DNA with Park Hyeonsu's.

963
00:53:36,296 --> 00:53:37,297
Yes, ma'am.

964
00:53:37,798 --> 00:53:39,216
[cell phone vibrating]

965
00:53:44,012 --> 00:53:45,013
Yes, sir.

966
00:53:46,056 --> 00:53:47,307
Yes, understood.

967
00:53:56,400 --> 00:53:57,693
[exhales deeply]

968
00:54:00,154 --> 00:54:01,321
[knock at door]

969
00:54:01,405 --> 00:54:02,406
Yes, come in.

970
00:54:04,032 --> 00:54:05,367
Detective Joo, have a seat.

971
00:54:05,451 --> 00:54:06,618
[door closes]

972
00:54:06,702 --> 00:54:09,288
I'm going fishing at dawn.
[chuckles softly]

973
00:54:09,955 --> 00:54:12,541
If I catch some big ones,
would you like one?

974
00:54:13,250 --> 00:54:16,503
They don't call me
the Sea King's eldest son for nothing.

975
00:54:16,587 --> 00:54:17,796
I'm all right, thank you.

976
00:54:19,965 --> 00:54:21,175
So,

977
00:54:22,468 --> 00:54:24,970
I hear Jin Isoo bought a house.

978
00:54:25,053 --> 00:54:26,263
Yes, sir.

979
00:54:26,346 --> 00:54:29,725
And you found five bodies inside?

980
00:54:30,309 --> 00:54:31,518
-Yes, sir.
-[gasps]

981
00:54:32,269 --> 00:54:34,980
Does he just make trouble
wherever he goes?

982
00:54:37,649 --> 00:54:39,568
-Is there nothing wrong with that?
-Pardon?

983
00:54:39,651 --> 00:54:43,280
I mean, is there anything
we can find fault with?

984
00:54:44,364 --> 00:54:47,784
Can a police officer
just buy up a house like that?

985
00:54:48,494 --> 00:54:49,786
There's no reason he can't.

986
00:54:50,871 --> 00:54:52,372
He's not breaking the law.

987
00:54:53,040 --> 00:54:54,875
We found five bodies there

988
00:54:54,958 --> 00:54:57,669
and prevented it
from becoming the perfect crime,

989
00:54:57,753 --> 00:54:58,795
so it's a good thing.

990
00:54:58,879 --> 00:55:00,631
How is that a good thing?

991
00:55:01,215 --> 00:55:02,216
Come on,

992
00:55:02,299 --> 00:55:05,719
I just want to make it to retirement
in peace, for God's sake.

993
00:55:10,140 --> 00:55:12,267
Should we hand this over
to Seoul Headquarters?

994
00:55:13,101 --> 00:55:14,895
It's a big case.

995
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:19,525
Don't worry, sir.
We'll catch whoever's behind this.

996
00:55:20,359 --> 00:55:22,027
[♪ gripping music playing]

997
00:55:24,112 --> 00:55:25,155
NO USABLE FINGERPRINTS

998
00:55:26,323 --> 00:55:28,242
SUSPECT, VICTIM

999
00:55:28,325 --> 00:55:30,786
PARK HYEONSU, AGE 34
KIM MINSEO, AGE 34

1000
00:55:32,037 --> 00:55:33,622
VICTIM KIM MINSEO'S HOUSE

1001
00:55:33,705 --> 00:55:34,957
SUSPECT PARK HYEONSU'S HOUSE

1002
00:55:38,252 --> 00:55:39,920
Ma'am, we got a match on the DNA.

1003
00:55:40,003 --> 00:55:41,046
It is Park Hyeonsu.

1004
00:55:42,673 --> 00:55:43,674
AUTOPSY REPORT

1005
00:55:45,592 --> 00:55:48,387
Who could have killed Park Hyeonsu?

1006
00:55:50,847 --> 00:55:52,266
Don't just think about him.

1007
00:55:53,267 --> 00:55:55,310
There are five bodies
killed by the same guy.

1008
00:55:59,231 --> 00:56:00,566
Then, was Park Hyeonsu

1009
00:56:01,775 --> 00:56:03,652
murdered by a serial killer?

1010
00:56:04,611 --> 00:56:05,612
No, wait.

1011
00:56:07,114 --> 00:56:08,156
Let's start over.

1012
00:56:15,414 --> 00:56:18,041
What if Park Hyeonsu wasn't the one
who killed Kim Minseo?

1013
00:56:18,917 --> 00:56:20,502
You're saying they're professionals?

1014
00:56:21,837 --> 00:56:22,838
Yes.

1015
00:56:25,465 --> 00:56:29,344
If Park Hyeonsu wasn't the one
who killed Kim Minseo...

1016
00:56:32,889 --> 00:56:34,516
It's the perfect crime.

1017
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:35,726
Right? Here, look.

1018
00:56:36,393 --> 00:56:38,562
Look. The target.

1019
00:56:38,645 --> 00:56:40,981
A victim to frame as the suspect.

1020
00:56:41,064 --> 00:56:43,400
If they kill the target and the suspect,

1021
00:56:43,483 --> 00:56:45,193
then make him go missing,

1022
00:56:45,777 --> 00:56:47,529
the case cannot be solved.

1023
00:56:48,989 --> 00:56:50,782
[Hyera] Five perfect crimes.

1024
00:56:51,491 --> 00:56:54,161
You need at least two people
to make this possible.

1025
00:56:54,828 --> 00:56:56,496
They're methodical and cold.

1026
00:56:56,580 --> 00:56:58,248
Park Hyeonsu would've been first,

1027
00:56:58,874 --> 00:57:00,167
since they sent those texts.

1028
00:57:02,753 --> 00:57:04,921
[Hyera] First, they overpowered
Park Hyeonsu.

1029
00:57:07,424 --> 00:57:09,134
One of them would've kept watch.

1030
00:57:14,723 --> 00:57:16,642
They sent the harassing messages.

1031
00:57:17,267 --> 00:57:18,685
-Hello.
-Hello, delivery.

1032
00:57:18,769 --> 00:57:20,437
Then, after killing the target...

1033
00:57:20,520 --> 00:57:21,813
-[muffled screaming]
-[flesh squelching]

1034
00:57:23,106 --> 00:57:24,691
[Hyera] ...they dressed up
as Park Hyeonsu.

1035
00:57:38,205 --> 00:57:39,206
[door beeps]

1036
00:57:45,545 --> 00:57:47,214
[muffled] Help me!

1037
00:57:47,881 --> 00:57:49,341
-[grunting]
-[flesh squelching]

1038
00:57:59,893 --> 00:58:01,603
Then they buried him and disappeared.

1039
00:58:01,687 --> 00:58:03,355
So they're professional killers?

1040
00:58:04,189 --> 00:58:05,190
Yes.

1041
00:58:05,857 --> 00:58:07,693
They must've been hired to do it.

1042
00:58:07,776 --> 00:58:09,361
[♪ ominous music playing]

1043
00:58:09,444 --> 00:58:12,322
Those bastards completely fooled me.

1044
00:58:12,406 --> 00:58:14,157
We need to start this case over.

1045
00:58:15,117 --> 00:58:18,120
The ones who attacked
you and Isoo must be the real culprits.

1046
00:58:19,454 --> 00:58:21,248
If they came to the house...

1047
00:58:21,331 --> 00:58:23,208
It means they killed someone else.

1048
00:58:24,251 --> 00:58:25,836
They were there to bury the body.

1049
00:58:34,594 --> 00:58:35,595
[suspect] Wait.

1050
00:58:37,097 --> 00:58:39,015
It's blood. [exclaims]

1051
00:58:39,474 --> 00:58:40,475
KILLER 1
JANG JAECHUN

1052
00:58:40,559 --> 00:58:41,560
It leaked.

1053
00:58:41,643 --> 00:58:42,644
KILLER 2
JO BEOMKI

1054
00:58:42,728 --> 00:58:43,729
What do we do?

1055
00:58:43,812 --> 00:58:45,355
[♪ tense music playing]

1056
00:58:45,439 --> 00:58:46,857
This is bad.

1057
00:58:48,567 --> 00:58:49,693
Taegwang.

1058
00:59:07,794 --> 00:59:08,879
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 3

1059
00:59:08,962 --> 00:59:10,213
THE KILLER OF KILLERS
YU TAEGWANG

1060
00:59:10,297 --> 00:59:12,299
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1061
00:59:34,821 --> 00:59:38,241
Special Cast.
Lee Hakju, Park Soi

1062
00:59:45,332 --> 00:59:46,792
[Taegwang] We got a new job.
Where are you?

1063
00:59:46,875 --> 00:59:48,293
-[Kyungjin] I got their location.
-[tires screech]

1064
00:59:48,543 --> 00:59:49,544
I need the chopper.

1065
00:59:49,628 --> 00:59:51,171
This is straight out of a soap opera.

1066
00:59:51,254 --> 00:59:52,464
You're Korean, right?

1067
00:59:52,547 --> 00:59:54,090
-I don't know.
-You don't know?

1068
00:59:54,883 --> 00:59:56,718
-Freeze.
-We're flying out at dawn.

1069
00:59:56,802 --> 00:59:59,387
[Hyera] They're ruthless killers,
so civilians could get hurt.

1070
00:59:59,471 --> 01:00:00,472
Beomki!

1071
01:00:01,056 --> 01:00:02,057
[Hyera] If we want to catch them...

1072
01:00:02,140 --> 01:00:03,391
Let's hire them to kill someone.

1073
01:00:03,767 --> 01:00:05,894
Is this how you normally investigate?

1074
01:00:07,103 --> 01:00:08,980
I won't let you down.

1075
01:00:09,064 --> 01:00:10,565
You were a real scumbag.

1076
01:00:10,649 --> 01:00:11,942
[Taegwang] We all go down together.

1077
01:00:12,025 --> 01:00:13,318
[Junyoung] So the perp's still here.

1078
01:00:14,861 --> 01:00:15,946
[gunshot]

1079
01:00:16,363 --> 01:00:17,739
Jin Isoo!

1080
01:00:22,285 --> 01:00:23,912
[♪ captivating music playing]

1081
01:00:41,555 --> 01:00:43,974
[Taegyun] Who is that?

1082
01:00:44,057 --> 01:00:45,851
Did we arrest a gang boss?

1083
01:00:47,519 --> 01:00:49,062
Is that Park?

1084
01:00:49,145 --> 01:00:50,188
[♪ quirky music playing]

1085
01:00:50,272 --> 01:00:51,273
Gosh.

1086
01:00:52,983 --> 01:00:54,526
What are they doing?

1087
01:00:54,609 --> 01:00:56,695
-[car door closes]
-I have no idea, sir.

1088
01:01:07,289 --> 01:01:08,707
Our district

1089
01:01:08,790 --> 01:01:10,876
is just strange overall.

1090
01:01:11,585 --> 01:01:13,587
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
